# Never upload local env files. Vercel's own env handling is the source of truth in prod, and a
# committed .env reaching the build both leaks secrets into the deployment and breaks the runtime:
# Next 16.2's Vercel builder wires the function to read a .env that isn't in the bundle, so every
# request dies with "failed to load env vars: EnvFileReadError(NotFound)". Keys live in `vercel env`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local tooling / OS noise — no reason to ship it.
.DS_Store
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.playwright-mcp/
